From ad6941a5ad11441ccb5d1ed5ee8cd54fc8fedbb2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yibo Wang <wyibo6109@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 05:28:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 77/79] virt: gunyah: Add runtime protected share (GuestAccept)
 ioctls

The host cannot map memory into a protected guest's stage-2 (the
hypervisor answers DENIED), so shared memory for a protected VM must
be accepted by the guest itself. Add the in-tree form of DroidVM's
out-of-tree gunyah_share model: the host SHAREs an RM memparcel and
hands the handle to the VMM; the guest ACCEPTs that handle at an IPA
of its choosing (RM MEM_ACCEPT) and RELEASEs it before the host
reclaims.

GH_VM_PROTECTED_SHARE pins a page-aligned userspace buffer
(FOLL_LONGTERM) and shares it as one memparcel (ACL: guest with the
requested access subset, host RWX), merging physically contiguous
runs; GH_VM_PROTECTED_SHARE_DMABUF does the same for a page-aligned
slice of a DMA-BUF, held by an attachment for exporters GUP cannot
pin; GH_VM_PROTECTED_UNSHARE reclaims by label. The RM refuses a
reclaim while the guest still holds its acceptance, so map MEM_INUSE
to -EBUSY (the Android source mapped it to -EINVAL) and leave the
parcel shared and pinned for the VMM to retry. Shares still live when
the VM fd is closed are reclaimed after the RM has reset the VM (the
reset drops the guest's acceptances); a parcel the RM will not return
is leaked rather than freed under a possibly live stage-2 mapping.
Labels carry bit 31 towards the RM so they cannot collide with
userspace-region parcel labels. Probe with GH_CAP_PROTECTED_SHARE.

Mainline addition, not from the android17-6.18 source; see
Documentation/virt/gunyah/port_adaptations.md. Host-side and
end-to-end tests in tools/virt/gunyah (gh_sharetest.py, and
gh_accepttest.py driving the gh_rmproxy.S bare-metal guest that
really accepts and releases), verified on the OnePlus Pad 4 (SM8850).

Signed-off-by: Yibo Wang <2024312277@stu.hit.edu.cn>
Co-Authored-By: Claude ZCode <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 06416a1eae89a50eaa4fc493ce57639cb65936c8)
